  {
    "id": "c002",
    "name": "Reinsurance relationship definition",
    "text": "Whereas Lincoln General, U.S, Auto and State. and County Matual Fire Insurance Company entered into a reinsurance relationship as detailed. in the General Agency Agreement and cotesponding, fully incorporated Texas Non-Standard Private Passenger Quota Share Reinsurance Agreement, each with effective dates of July 1, 2002 (the “2002 GAA” and “2002 Q/S,” respeotively); the General Agency Agreement and comesponding, fully incorporated Texas Non-Standard Private Passenger Quota Share Reinsurance Agreement, each with effective dates of July 1, 2003 (the “2003 GAA” and “2003 Q/S,” respectively); and all addenda to each those agreements, including, but not lonited to, Addendum No. 1 to the 2003 Q/S (with an effective date of July 1, 2004), Addendum No. 2 to the 2003 Q/S (with an effective date of September 30, 2005), and Addendum No. 3 to the 2003 Q/S (with an cffective date of January 1, © 2007)(hereinafter “the reinsurance relationship”);"
  },
  {
    "id": "c003",
    "name": "Lawsuit definition",
    "text": "Whereas Linooln General sued U.S. Auto, Gamma, CSi, Alpha, Doug Maxwell, Santa Fe and Jim Maxwell in the above entitled lawsuit (the “Lawsnit”); and"
  },
  {
    "id": "c004",
    "name": "I. Loss Portfolio Transfer",
    "text": "I, ‘Santa Fe to Reinsure Lincoln General. On or before June 30, 2009, Lincoln General and Santa Fe shall enter into a Loss Portfolio Transfer Reinsurance Agreement (“LPT”) whereby Santa Fe shall reinsure, indemnify, assume, and be liabie to Lincoln General for all past and futute losses, payments, risks, and habilities of Lincoln General arising in connection with the 2002 GAA, 2002 Q/S, 2003 GAA, 2003 Q/S, and all addenila to those agreements, whether or not such losses, payments, risks, and liabilities are known or can be ascertained at this time."
