{"judgments": [
  {"clause_id": "c001",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The parenthetical defined terms are mangled: \"CSi Agency Services, Ino. (“CS”)\" defines the short name \"CS\" while every operative section uses \"CSi,\" and \"Alpha Partners, Ltd, Alpha”)\" opens no quotation mark. The mechanical error leaves the identity of the defined parties to be construed against sections III and X, which impose or release obligations by short name.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.13}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c002",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The recital defines \"the reinsurance relationship\" to include \"all addenda to each those agreements, including, but not limited to,\" three named addenda, so the enumerated specifics do not bound the catch-all. Which further addenda are swept into the defined relationship, and thus into the LPT obligation in section I, is left open.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.16}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c003", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c004",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The obligation is to \"enter into a Loss Portfolio Transfer Reinsurance Agreement\" whose terms, premium, conditions and form are nowhere stated, so the provision is an agreement to make a future agreement. A court must decide whether \"shall enter into\" is an enforceable promise or leaves essential terms open.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.52},
     {"issue": "Section IX describes the same document as \"a mutually agreeable reinsurance agreement/LPT\" and provides a remedy for the parties being \"not able to complete\" it, which cannot be squared with section I's unconditional \"shall enter into\" by June 30, 2009. Whether failure to execute the LPT is a breach of section I or merely triggers section IX must be construed.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.44}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c005",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The carve-out for \"payments completed prior to May 4, 2009\" is measured by a definition (section I's \"completed\" sentence) keyed solely to checks \"dated and issued by Santa Fe,\" leaving pre-May 4 payments made by Lincoln General or out of the ZBA unaddressed. The two sentences read together do not say who bears those payments.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.24}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c006",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"Completed\" is defined by the conjunctive test \"dated and issued by Santa Fe,\" which gives no answer when a check is dated before May 4, 2009 but issued after (or the reverse). The provision also fixes the test only for checks issued by Santa Fe, not by any other party.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.27}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c007",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "Permission to use the ZBA ends \"until the LPT is executed, but no later than June 30, 2009,\" yet section IX expressly contemplates that the LPT may never be executed, leaving no mechanism for funding claims after June 30, 2009. The two provisions cannot both be given effect without construing which controls.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.22}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c008",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"[T]he date of execution\" is unspecified — execution of the LPT or execution of this Memorandum of Understanding — and the same phrase reappears in the following reimbursement sentence. The cut-off for ZBA checks therefore has two readings on the face of the sentence.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.24}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c009",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The reimbursement duty is stated with no time for performance and no interest, so when Santa Fe must repay ZBA draws is left at large. \"[T]he date of execution\" likewise takes its meaning only from the preceding sentence.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.15}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c010",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The $3 million is said to be \"partial security\" and expressly \"not ... a limitation on those obligations,\" but the final sentence of the same section caps posted security at \"not exceed $3 million.\" Whether Santa Fe can ever be required to post more than $3 million must be construed between the two.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.20}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c011",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "Option (b) requires \"an A rated reinsurer\" without naming the rating agency or the date the rating is measured, and option (a) requires \"other investments acceptable to Lincoln General\" with no standard of acceptability. Both terms leave the sufficiency of the security to one party's undefined judgment.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.29}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c012",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The requirement that Lincoln General \"be permitted to participate in the drafting and wording of the agreement\" sets no measure of participation or of what terms the reinsurance agreement must contain. Whether a reinsurance placement satisfies section II therefore turns on an unstated standard.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.20}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c013",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "This sentence caps the collateral at \"not exceed $3 million\" for \"the amount of future losses forecast,\" which conflicts with the opening of section II stating the $3 million is \"partial security\" and \"not ... a limitation on those obligations.\" A court must decide whether the cap limits Santa Fe's security duty after a reinsurer default.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.22}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c014",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "Release of trust funds whenever market value merely \"is greater than\" Santa Fe's estimated remaining liability cannot be squared with section II(a), under which the escrowed funds \"shall only be able to be withdrawn with Lincoln General's consent\" and secure the whole $3 million. Whether the entire corpus, or only the excess, may be released is unstated.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.27}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c015",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"This release shall be performed annually\" is mandatory, while the preceding sentence says the funds \"may be released\" — permissive — only if a market-value test is met. The two sentences of section II cannot both be given effect without construing whether the annual release is compulsory, and from what date the year runs.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.24}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c016",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "Santa Fe's duty to fund \"all activities\" for claims under the 2002 and 2003 agreements carries no start date, whereas section I excludes from Santa Fe's liability any payment \"completed prior to May 4, 2009.\" Whether section III reaches pre-May 4, 2009 claim activity must be construed against that exclusion.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.24}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c017",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The catch-all \"any other expenses related to claims investigation, settlement, contesting, and handling\" sits against an enumerated list of claim payments, attorney's fees and legal expenses, leaving its outer bound unfixed. Whether it reaches, for example, Lincoln General's own litigation or administrative costs is open.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.24}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c018",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The preservation of \"any obligations of U.S. Auto, Gamma, or any other defendant\" cannot be squared with section X, under which the contemplated settlement agreement will \"provide for releases of all Defendants\" upon Santa Fe's performance. Which provision governs the other defendants' continuing liability must be construed.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.28}
   ]}
]}

