   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The installment schedule begins January 2, 2010 and runs to 2014 regardless of whether the LPT and settlement agreement are ever executed, while section IX provides that if those documents are not completed Lincoln General's remedy \"shall be to refile the lawsuit.\" Whether the note payments survive a section IX failure is unaddressed.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.16}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c021",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The note must be \"in a form substantially similar to Exhibit A,\" but no Exhibit A is attached to the executed Memorandum of Understanding. The referenced form is missing from the instrument, and \"substantially similar\" supplies no standard in its absence.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.25}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c022",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The parties' stipulation that the Memorandum is \"sufficiently definite to allow the parties to sue for its enforcement\" cannot be squared with section IX, which limits Lincoln General's remedy for non-completion to refiling the lawsuit. Whether suit on the Memorandum or refiling the dismissed case is available must be construed between the two.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.54},
     {"issue": "\"[S]ufficiently definite to allow the parties to sue for its enforcement\" is a recitation of a legal conclusion, and the provision does not say which obligations it is definite as to. Whether the parties can contract themselves out of indefiniteness as to sections I and X is left to construction.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.32}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c023",
   "issues": [
